  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Hoola (Korean Rummy). 2-5 players, 52-card deck. Deal: 7 cards anticlockwise. Turn: Draw stock or claim discard. Meld: Sets (3+ rank) or Runs (3+ consecutive, same suit). Sevens meld solo. Knock: End round when points <15-20. Scoring: K(13) Q(12) J(11) 10-8(face) 7(7) 6-2(face) A(1). Win: Lowest points or empty hand.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Hoola, the Korean rummy game. Meld sets (3+ same rank) and runs (3+ consecutive, same suit). Sevens are specialâ€”meld solo or double penalty if caught. Draw from stock or battle for the discard. Once your points are low enough, knock to end the round. Lowest points wins!',
    objective: "Win by melding all cards in your hand or having the lowest point total when someone 'knocks'.",
    gameplay: "1. Players draw from the stock or claim the discard.\n2. **Battle**: If multiple players want the discard, there is a priority system (usually the next player in order has first right).\n3. **Melding**: - **Sets**: 3 or 4 cards of the same rank. - **Runs**: 3+ consecutive cards of the same suit (Cyclic: K-A-2 is allowed). - **Sevens**: A single 7 can be melded alone.\n4. **Blast**: Winning with a specific combination involving 7s or a clean sweep of the hand recorded as a 'Blast' (double points).",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hoola.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: - Face cards: 10-13 pts.',
      "Winning condition: Win by melding all cards in your hand or having the lowest point total when someone 'knocks'.",
    ],
